# Working on {{skillName}}

This file is for people and agents changing the skill. To use the skill, see [SKILL.md](SKILL.md) and
[README.md](README.md).

## What is in the repository

| Path                | Purpose                                                         |
| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `SKILL.md`          | The skill: frontmatter and the instructions Claude follows      |
| `README.md`         | Install and usage for people                                    |
| `CLAUDE.md`         | Pointers for Claude Code when it opens this repository          |
| `__tests__/`        | Jest tests                                                      |
| `eslint.config.cjs` | ESLint 10 flat config; Prettier handles formatting              |
| `lefthook.yml`      | Git hooks: lint and test before commit, branch name before push |
{{#hasShellScripts}}
| `skill/scripts/`    | Shell scripts the skill runs; checked by ShellCheck             |
{{/hasShellScripts}}
{{#hasBatsTests}}
| `tests/`            | BATS integration tests                                          |
{{/hasBatsTests}}

The tooling comes from [ls-skill-scaffold](https://github.com/lightspeedwp/ls-skill-scaffold). Change shared
tooling there first, then bring it here.

## Rules for changes

- Keep the frontmatter `description` in `SKILL.md` under 1,024 characters. Say when to use the skill and when
  not to.
- Add or update an eval in `evals/` for any change in behaviour.
- Add tests for new code. Coverage below {{testCoverageThreshold}}% fails `npm test`.

## Checks

```bash
npm install
npm run lint:all
npm test
```

Branch names follow `{type}/{scope}-{title}`, for example `feat/skill-add-preview`.
